    "difficulty": "EASY",
    "stem": "Find the derivative of \\(7^x\\) w.r.t. \\(x^7\\).",
    "solution": "Let \\(u = 7^x\\) and \\(v = x^7\\), then we have to find \\(\\frac{du}{dv}\\).\n\\(\\therefore \\frac{du}{dv} = \\frac{\\frac{du}{dx}}{\\frac{dv}{dx}}\\) ... (I)\nNow, \\(u = 7^x\\)\nDifferentiate w.r.t. \\(x\\)\n\\(\\frac{du}{dx} = \\frac{d}{dx}(7^x) = 7^x \\log 7\\) ... (II)\nAnd, \\(v = x^7\\)\nDifferentiate w.r.t. \\(x\\)\n\\(\\frac{dv}{dx} = \\frac{d}{dx}(x^7) = 7x^6\\) ... (III)\nSubstituting (II) and (III) in (I) we get,\n\\(\\therefore \\frac{du}{dv} = \\frac{7^x \\log 7}{7x^6}\\)"
  },
  {
